ylanilinium"},{"x":"−9.3","w":"2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium"}],"t":"Quinuclidinium","fig":{"m":150},"ex":"Quinuclidinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 11 in water. The tied-back ring leaves the lone pair exposed.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"8.36"},{"x":"5.2","w":"N,N-Dimethylanilinium"},{"x":"−9.3","w":"2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium"},{"x":"11","w":"Quinuclidinium"}],"t":"Morpholinium","fig":{"m":151},"ex":"Morpholinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 8.36 in water. The ring oxygen pulls electron density from nitrogen.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"7.38"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"},{"x":"4.6","w":"Anilinium"},{"x":"11","w":"Quinuclidinium"}],"t":"N-Methylmorpholinium","fig":{"m":152},"ex":"N-Methylmorpholinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 7.38 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"8.82"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"},{"x":"−10","w":"Protonated benzonitrile"},{"x":"11.05","w":"Diisopropylammonium"}],"t":"DABCO-H⁺","fig":{"m":153},"ex":"DABCO-H⁺: the highlighted proton has pKa 8.82 in water. First protonation. The second is 2.97.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"p