anic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"5.2"},{"x":"8.36","w":"Morpholinium"},{"x":"10.6","w":"Ethylammonium"},{"x":"−10","w":"Protonated benzonitrile"}],"t":"N,N-Dimethylanilinium","f":"C₆H₅NMe₂H⁺","fig":{"m":157},"ex":"N,N-Dimethylanilinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 5.2 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"0.78"},{"x":"12","w":"Proton sponge-H⁺"},{"x":"5.21","w":"Pyridinium"},{"x":"8.36","w":"Morpholinium"}],"t":"Diphenylammonium","f":"Ph₂NH₂⁺","fig":{"m":158},"ex":"Diphenylammonium: the highlighted proton has pKa 0.78 in water. Two rings delocalise the lone pair.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"4.16"},{"x":"0.72","w":"2-Chloropyridinium"},{"x":"8.12","w":"Hydrazinium"},{"x":"−10","w":"Protonated benzonitrile"}],"t":"2-Naphthylammonium","fig":{"m":159},"ex":"2-Naphthylammonium: the highlighted proton has pKa 4.16 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"−9.3"},{"x":"8.82","w":"DABCO-H⁺"},{"x":"6.75","w":"2,6-Lutidinium"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"}],"t":"2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium","fig":{"m":160},"ex":"2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium: the highlighted proton has pKa −9.3 in water. Three nitro groups leave the amine almost non-basic.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"12"},{"x":"5.2","w":"N,N-Dimethylanilinium"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"},{"x":"7.38","w":"N-Methylmorpholinium"}],"t":"Proton sponge-H⁺","fig":{"m":161},"ex":"Proton sponge-H⁺: the highlighted proton has pKa 12 in water. Protonation relieves the clash between the two lone pairs.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"5.21"},{"x":"8.82","w":"DABCO-H⁺"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"},{"x":"12","w":"Proton sponge-H⁺"}],"t":"Pyridinium","f":"C₅H₅NH⁺","fig":{"m":17},"ex":"Pyridinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 5.21 in water. Also 3.4 in DMSO. PPTS is its tosylate salt.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"6.75"},{"x":"9.2","w":"DMAP-H⁺"},{"x":"−10","w":"Protonated benzonitrile"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"}],"t":"2,6-Lutidinium","fig":{"m":162},"ex":"2,6-Lutidinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 6.75 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"4.95"},{"x":"0.72","w":"2-Chloropyridinium"},{"x":"11.05","w":"Diisopropylammonium"},{"x":"8.12","w":"Hydrazinium"}],"t":"2,6-Di-tert-butylpyridinium","fig":{"m":163},"ex":"2,6-Di-tert-butylpyridinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 4.95 in water. The bulk blocks solvation of the cation, so it is less basic than lutidine.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"0.72"},{"x":"5.21","w":"Pyridinium"},{"x":"12","w":"Proton sponge-H⁺"},{"x":"8.82","w":"DABCO-H⁺"}],"t":"2-Chloropyridinium","fig":{"m":164},"ex":"2-Chloropyridinium: the highlighted proton has pKa 0.72 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"9.2"},{"x":"5.2","w":"N,N-Dimethylanilinium"},{"x":"0.72","w":"2-Chloropyridinium"},{"x":"−10","w":"Protonated benzonitrile"}],"t":"DMAP-H⁺","fig":{"m":165},"ex":"DMAP-H⁺: the highlighted proton has pKa 9.2 in water. The NMe₂ group pushes electron density onto the ring nitrogen.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"6.95"},{"x":"4.95","w":"2,6-Di-tert-butylpyridinium"},{"x":"10.6","w":"Ethylammonium"},{"x":"0.78","w":"Diphenylammonium"}],"t":"Imidazolium","fig":{"m":19},"ex":"Imidazolium: the highlighted proton has pKa 6.95 in water.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"pKa value","a":"What is the pKa of the highlighted proton in water?","o":[{"x":"−10"},{"x":"4.6","w":"Anilinium"},{"x":"7.38","w":"N-Methylmorpholinium"},{"x":"10.75","w":"Triethylammonium"}],"t":"Protonated benzonitrile","f":"C₆H₅C≡NH⁺","fig":{"m":166},"ex":"Protonated benzonitrile: the highlighted proton has pKa −10 in water. The sp nitrogen holds its lone pair very tightly.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"Strongest acid","a":"Which of these is the strongest acid in water?","o":[{"m":166,"x":"Protonated benzonitrile","v":"pKa −10"},{"m":164,"x":"2-Chloropyridinium","v":"pKa 0.72"},{"m":154,"x":"Ethylenediammonium","v":"pKa 6.9"},{"m":161,"x":"Proton sponge-H⁺","v":"pKa 12"}],"ex":"pKa in water: Protonated benzonitrile −10 < 2-Chloropyridinium 0.72 < Ethylenediammonium 6.9 < Proton sponge-H⁺ 12. The lowest pKa belongs to the strongest acid.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"Strongest acid","a":"Which of these is the strongest acid in water?","o":[{"m":160,"x":"2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium","v":"pKa −9.3"},{"m":158,"x":"Diphenylammonium","v":"pKa 0.78"},{"m":19,"x":"Imidazolium","v":"pKa 6.95"},{"m":150,"x":"Quinuclidinium","v":"pKa 11"}],"ex":"pKa in water: 2,4,6-Trinitroanilinium −9.3 < Diphenylammonium 0.78 < Imidazolium 6.95 < Quinuclidinium 11. The lowest pKa belongs to the strongest acid.","lk":[{"h":"Source","l":[["Evans pKa table (Ripin & Evans, ACS Organic Division, 2024)","https://organicchemistrydata.org/hansreich/resources/pka/pka_data/evans_pKa_table.pdf"]]}]},{"s":"pka","k":"Strongest acid","a":"Which of these is the strongest acid in water?","o":[{"m":166,"x":"Protonated benzonitrile","v":"pKa −10"},{"m":164,"x":